{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>They shall teach Your judgments to Jacob</b> — that they spread throughout all Israel to learn Torah. And so Jacob said, ואפיצם בישראל (and I will spread them in Israel). ישימו קטורה (they shall place incense). In gematria, like מעשיר." "<b>And whole-offering</b> — two times. וכליל על מזבחך (and whole-offering upon Your altar). אז תחפוץ זבחי צדק עולה וכליל (then You desire sacrifices of righteousness, burnt-offering and whole-offering). Even though a non-priest offers on a bamah, it is not זבחי צדק (sacrifices of righteousness) except that which is brought inside by a priest. And this is וכליל על מזבחך, אז תחפוץ זבחי צדק עולה וכליל."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {0 "The verse quoted as Jacob's words, ואפיצם בישראל, appears to allude to Jacob's blessing of Levi in Genesis 49:7 (אפיצם בישראל); the prefixed vav may reflect the Ba'al HaTurim's reading or a variant tradition."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:11:28.522967506Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}